WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.369
Good morning, John. Last week I was in Amsterdam and as usual when I go someplace that is not my home, I'm struck

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.590
by all of the little differences like all the bikes and the trains and the trams where in my town

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.920
almost everybody gets around by car. It's easy to

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.620
say that this is a question of circumstance

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.180
and of course it is.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.740
In Amsterdam, it's dense the roads are old and narrow and the country is flat and isn't covered in snow

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.020
half the year, like it is here in Montana but it's

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.260
also a question of choice.

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:32.459
Individuals making decisions in establishing and following norms. In Amsterdam, even if it's faster to take a bus, even if it's raining and gross, people

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:39.149
still bike because that's what you do, and since so many people do ,everything is built for bikes and trams and trains.

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:44.760
While I imagine trying to find parking would be a miserable terrible disaster. I don't actually know though, how these

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:51.500
norms get established. I imagine that they are things that just fit, things that simply make sense to the people

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.360
who have come together to make a place. Norms that, make them feel good and

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:02.460
valued and healthy and satisfied. The blending of story into place, into groups that's the thing that I thought a lot

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:09.240
about this year at Vidcon EU because it's also the story of online communities which is what Vidcon ultimately is about. At

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.080
Vidcon EU this year

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.189
We weren't able to have a fan component for a bunch of reasons that I'll put on the screen right now if you're curious.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.239
But it was still able to be that kind of cultural exploration, we get a chance to ask

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.580
where our ideas come from what stories, we are telling to ourselves and to each other and whether they're

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.779
good stories. Having the community there I think makes that even better which is why I came

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:33.869
away, from Vidcon EU so excited for Anaheim and Australia later this year. I'm working on what I think are

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:39.688
some pretty, good speeches for those Vidcon's about defining success and some of the strategies that I find really work

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:42.929
when trying to figure out what kind of content is going to get attention

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:46.499
and be successful but, also not be bad for the people watching it. I'm excited about

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.500
My panels and also to do an old-school

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.369
acoustic set to close out the whole event in Anaheim. I guess being a founder has its

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:59.460
advantages. I'm really proud of Vidcon. Proud of people, who take their stories seriously and who let

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.269
Them change and become messy and complex. A couple of weeks ago on our new

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.530
Podcast, Delete This, Katherine and i were talking about how, the messiness of stories can

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:15.669
make it hard to love something a hundred percent but, maybe loving something 100 percent isn't right. Maybe it starts with

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.100
joy, and ends with joy but joy that

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:24.009
also has care and concern and thought mixed in and if we're not doing it that way, I don't even know

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:29.470
if that's right, which is why I love Vidcon and also why I love my new podcast where Catherine reviews

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.949
my twitter feed and if you, want to find out more about those things there's links

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.110
and maybe even some coupon codes in the description.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:40.239
Any opportunity to examine the stories I tell myself is something I want more of in my life.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.839
Taking an hour every week to go through my twitter feed with someone who cares about

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.550
me a lot is a great way to do that and so is traveling to a new place and making a bunch of cool

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:54.249
time-lapse videos. And so is getting together to celebrate and contemplate with a bunch of people

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:59.020
who care about, love and are excited about and also worried about a lot of the same things as me

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.540
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

